capability ui/app-menu  the application's menu of macOS: About, Settings, Services, Hide, Hide Others, Show All, Quit, and the program's items that stand there
  heroes  ui.set_role, ui.MenuRole
  go      -
  rust    tauri::menu::PredefinedMenuItem::about, tauri::menu::PredefinedMenuItem::services, tauri::menu::PredefinedMenuItem::hide, tauri::menu::PredefinedMenuItem::hide_others, tauri::menu::PredefinedMenuItem::show_all, tauri::menu::PredefinedMenuItem::quit
  python  -
  wx      wxMenuBar (OSXGetAppleMenu), the stock identifiers wxID_ABOUT, wxID_PREFERENCES, wxID_EXIT
  note    on macOS the arm's application menu holds the system's Services, Hide, Hide Others and Show All, and an item of the program's with a role stands in About's, Settings' (Command+,) or Quit's place, hidden where it was made, its choosing told as itself; without one, About shows the system's panel and Quit asks every window to close; Windows and Linux have no such menu and keep the item where it was made (their arms pending)

